{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>If in My statutes etc., and five of you shall pursue etc.</b> This is difficult, for this calculation is not consistent: five against a hundred means one pursues twenty, and a hundred against ten thousand means one pursues a hundred. And one may answer that the prayer of the congregation is superior. Alternatively, this is what it says: 'and a hundred of you' — meaning a hundred groups of five, [so] ten thousand will pursue, which is also one to twenty. However, that calculation in the portion Ha'azinu, where it is written ״איכה ירדוף אחד אלף ושנים יניסו רבבה״, yields one pursuing five thousand, and furthermore it is difficult from there, for we say that the measure of good is greater than the measure of punishment — and superficially there [in Ha'azinu] it means one from the nations will pursue a thousand from Israel, and two [will pursue] ten thousand, whereas here, regarding good, it says only one from Israel will pursue twenty. And it seems to me that there too it means that the pursuers are Israel and the pursued are the idolaters, and it refers back to what precedes it: ״חכמו ישכילו זאת האומות ישכילו זאת יבינו לאחריתם״ — how it was that one pursuer from Israel [pursued] a thousand idolaters, namely Samson, who killed a thousand Philistines, as it is written ״בלחי החמור הכיתי אלף איש״. And ״ושנים יניסו רבבה״ — this is Jonathan. And had their Rock not sold them to the nations at the hands of these, and HaShem delivered them — and if so, it was for them to understand that HaShem wrought all this. Alternatively: here it speaks of pursuing and killing, as it is written ״ונפלו אויביכם לפניכם לחרב״; but there it is written ״יניסו״ — they flee, but do not kill."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The text ונטרו appears obscure; rendered hyper-literally as 'and had [their Rock] not sold them,' reading ונטרו as a variant or corruption related to the paraphrase of Deuteronomy 32:30. The reference to Jonathan alludes to 1 Samuel 14."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:48.326869461Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}